# SABOTAGE: issue #36 / ADR-038 §6.2 — the rate-limit bucket name loses its per-subject
# VALUE: `"{surface}:{kind}:{value}"` becomes `"{surface}:{kind}"`, so every `kid` on a
# surface shares ONE counter. This is the isolation RP-J-13 now depends on, removed at the
# seam rather than in the test: a single noisy cockpit consumes every other app's heartbeat
# budget, and the §4.4a starvation mitigation that gives each app its own budget is gone.
#
# Flips RP-J-13's PRECONDITION CONTROL, and nothing else in that suite: the arm plants the
# prior traffic the pre-fix version silently assumed away — another cockpit's kid driven PAST
# the limit in the same window — and then asserts its OWN bucket is still below limit before
# it sends anything. With the value dropped from the key, the planted flood lands in this
# app's bucket and the `refute over_limit?(:fleet_heartbeat, :kid, app_id)` control fires.
#
# VERIFIED, and the point of the patch: against the PRE-FIX test file this same sabotage runs
# 14/14 GREEN. One kid per test and a `reset/0` between tests make a collapsed key
# indistinguishable from a per-kid one — which is exactly why the old arm could take its
# precondition on faith and go red by seed instead. The control this patch flips is the new
# thing, not a restatement of an existing red.
#
# NOT TOUCHED: the limits themselves (`@default_limits`, `limit_for/1`), the fixed-window
# algorithm and its wall-clock window index (issue #36's root cause — the fix pins the window
# open in the test, and this patch leaves that alone), `check/3`/`over_limit?/3`/
# `record_failure/3`/`bump/3`'s return contracts, and the charge-only-on-{:ok,_} BLOCKER-1
# ordering in `CockpitIngress`.
#
# Changes one function head + body, so the module still compiles under
# --warnings-as-errors (the unused parameter is spelled `_value`).
#
# Out of scope for TEST_FILES but worth stating: this is a key-discipline regression the auth
# (`Samen.Web.Auth.RateLimitTest`), webhook and public-status suites ALSO catch — 8 further
# reds across samen_web. Those prove per-key isolation for their own surfaces; none of them
# covers the fleet heartbeat bucket, which is why RP-J-13 needs its own control.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/fleet_ingress_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RP-J-13: over-limit is a byte-identical 429 for a KNOWN kid
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/rate_limit.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/rate_limit.ex
index fc6558a..bab66ef 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/rate_limit.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/rate_limit.ex
@@ -163,7 +163,11 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.RateLimit do
   # The non-PII key discipline (§6.2): surface:kind:value — value is provider/ip/bidx/id.
   # Hammer stamps the fixed window internally; this string is the "bucket name" the
   # non-PII probe (done-criterion 2) greps + inspects at runtime.
-  defp bucket(surface, kind, value), do: "#{surface}:#{kind}:#{value}"
+  # SABOTAGE (issue #36 / ADR-038 §6.2): the per-subject VALUE is dropped from the bucket
+  # name, so every `kid` (and every IP, bidx, credential id) on a surface shares ONE counter.
+  # Each individual test still looks right — one kid per test, reset between tests — while a
+  # single noisy cockpit now consumes every other app's heartbeat budget.
+  defp bucket(surface, kind, _value), do: "#{surface}:#{kind}"
 
   @doc """
   The configured `{limit, window_ms}` for `surface` (config override or the
